WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:10.700
Visual distress signals are required on coastal waters: the ocean, the Gulf, and connected bays and sounds until they narrow to less than two miles wide.

2
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.900
A boat sixteen feet or longer must carry signals for both day and night.

3
00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.875
Follow the table.

4
00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:20.875
Red hand flares count for day and night.

5
00:00:21.125 --> 00:00:24.250
So do red meteor and parachute flares.

6
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.875
Orange smoke is for day only.

7
00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:28.375
Why?

8
00:00:29.375 --> 00:00:31.550
You can’t see smoke in the dark.

9
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.225
The orange distress flag is also day only.

10
00:00:35.475 --> 00:00:38.675
And the electric SOS light is night only.

11
00:00:38.925 --> 00:00:41.675
So three red flares cover you for both.

12
00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:48.275
Or you can pair a flag for day with an electric light for night, and carry no pyrotechnics at all.

13
00:00:48.525 --> 00:00:54.575
One date to remember: pyrotechnic signals expire forty-two months after manufacture.

14
00:00:54.825 --> 00:00:58.525
And never fire one except in a real emergency.
